# Finviz Elite EXPORT API token only.
#
# Which one: the UUID in `auth=` on an Elite export URL, e.g.
#   https://elite.finviz.com/export/screener?...&auth=<THIS>
#   https://elite.finviz.com/export/quote?t=MSFT&auth=<THIS>
#
# How to get it: log into Elite → Screener → Export → copy `auth=` from that link.
# Official docs (while logged in): https://elite.finviz.com/api_explanation.ashx
#
# If your account page lists several API keys, use the Screener / export one that
# appears on /export/screener and /export/quote. We use ONE key for screener,
# quote history, and options pages.
#
# NOT this: .ASPXAUTH login cookie, Google OAuth, password, free Finviz, or a
# key that only works on portfolio/news if it differs from screener export.
#
# Never commit this file. Set the same value as GitHub Actions secret FINVIZ_AUTH_TOKEN.
FINVIZ_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Optional. Default: optionable only. Universe is config/watchlist.txt (`t=`), not avg-vol/price filters.
# FINVIZ_SCREENER_FILTERS=sh_opt_option
# FINVIZ_WATCHLIST=config/watchlist.txt

# SNAPSHOT_ROOT=snapshots
# FINVIZ_CACHE=.cache/finviz

# Optional triage + phone push (python -m xtrading.analyst). Same names as the
# GitHub Actions secrets. Without ANTHROPIC_API_KEY the push is a headline only.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# NTFY_TOPIC=            # unguessable topic name, e.g. desk-9f2c7a41b6
# NTFY_URL=https://ntfy.sh
# NTFY_TOKEN=            # only for a protected topic / self-hosted server
